{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"qaoa-finite-size","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:6b1c59ab234bbf188aa4d4b6025767453ec328d381122b018700a897280799ad/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03","passage_ref":"sha256:a19893f62d1211681ed0cb9cbb8bb454214d97f231f6a6d091b6f198fca35a89/papers/long.md/sha256:6b1c59ab234bbf188aa4d4b6025767453ec328d381122b018700a897280799ad/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&paper=long&passage=qaoa-finite-size","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&paper=long&passage=qaoa-finite-size","span":{"end_byte":237791,"end_line":5139,"start_byte":234673,"start_line":5069},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&view=arguments&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&view=arguments&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&ref=sha256%3A3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.later_finite_size_comparison","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The displayed finite estimate is quoted from the later arXiv:2609.40309v1 Corollary S3.1; the growing-depth consequence is the authored elementary deduction log log T_p=4p log p+O(p+log p) with epsilon_p=exp(-p^2). For SK, c_2=1/sqrt(2) matches the unordered-pair expectation after an independent mean-zero scalar diagonal offset. This does not show that the earlier near-optimal constructed words share a uniform angle bound, supply angle-selection complexity, or establish a growing-depth measurement tail. It is standalone context, not a prerequisite of the earlier SK QAOA construction or a selected formal endpoint.","citation_ids":["qaoa_finite_size_corollary","authored_bounded_angle_depth_comparison"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"A later finite-size estimate for a bounded-angle class","locator":"Corollary S3.1, printed pp.46–47, equations (S3.1)–(S3.4), with cost-angle convention (S3.7). Statement inspected; full cavity proof not independently checked. Authored consequence: long §11.5.","source_id":"qaoa_finite_size_2026","statement":"For the source ordered-tuple Gaussian finite-degree mixture xi(t)=sum_q c_q^2 t^q, a depth p>=1 word with every cost angle bounded in absolute value by Gamma>0, and x>0 with xi(2),xi′(1),xi′′(33)<=x and Gamma^2 p^2 x>=1, set B_p=256p^4(2e Gamma^2 p^2 x)^p, E_p=70 Gamma^2 p^2 x+p log(2), R_p=(2E_p/log(2))^(2p). For 0<epsilon<=4 Gamma p x min(exp(-1/2),2^(-(8p^2+3)/100)), the disorder-averaged energy error |nu_n-nu_infinity| is at most epsilon whenever n>=T_p=max{2^(8p^2+3) B_p (2^(deg(xi)+4) Gamma^2 p^2 x^2/epsilon^2)^R_p [2 log_2(4 Gamma p x/epsilon)+deg(xi)]^2,16 Gamma p x/epsilon}. No mixer-angle bound is imposed. Consequently, for fixed mixture,Gamma,x, deterministic words with p(n)→infinity, one common cost-angle bound Gamma, and p(n)log p(n)=o(log log n) satisfy |nu_n(W_n)-nu_infinity(W_n)|<=exp(-p(n)^2) eventually.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:554a44b7dc6299455edf7e8dde58749352c97cd9306e982a0c0bcfc12925e10a","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"evidence_ids","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","id":"field:78d2fdd2470a9f7837e2771214a7191062cf2763e43a89d15ffb2ca748a66949","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:814081b74964ed6fb96f1a6e64813924e35d8c99235806b59a27623d4e0ceba2","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/citations/qaoa_finite_size_corollary"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_compari